Applied on top of vite@8.2.2.patch. vite main still has this race, so it carries no fixedIn.

The deps optimizer could keep bundling into cacheDir after server.close() resolved:
- onCrawlEnd() detaches optimizationResult before awaiting it, so close() neither cancels nor waits for that run;
- a scan that finishes after close() still starts a fresh run;
- a run's cancel() deleted deps_temp_* while bundle.write() was still writing into it;
- runOptimizer(preRunResult) returns early once closed without cancelling the run it was handed,
  so a finished deps_temp_* folder stayed in the cache.
A caller that removes cacheDir after close() then gets "Failed to write file in .../deps_temp_*" as an
unhandled rejection from onCrawlEnd(). close() now cancels and waits for every run that is neither
committed nor cleaned up, cancel() lets the write finish before it removes the folder, and a scan never
starts a run once the optimizer is closed.

